<p dir="auto">Add interactive examples to <code class="notranslate">sin()</code> and <code class="notranslate">cos()</code> CSS functions.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>
<p dir="auto">On September 2025, both <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/sin" rel="nofollow">sin()</a> and <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/cos" rel="nofollow">cos()</a> will become <a href="https://web.dev/baseline" rel="nofollow">baseline widely available</a>, yet both MDN articles have minimal information about the functions.</p>
<p dir="auto">The interactive examples interface enhances the learning experience by allowing visitors to modify the code and see the results. This is a more instructive way to understand how these CSS functions work.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Related pull requests</h3>
